# VPN / Network privacy
# Core VPN support — NetworkManager manages OpenVPN (.ovpn) and WireGuard (.conf)
# profiles; `hyprconf vpn` wraps nmcli around them. networkmanager-openvpn is the
# plugin NM needs to run imported OpenVPN profiles (e.g. ProtonVPN .ovpn configs);
# wireguard-tools provides wg/wg-quick so nmcli can import WireGuard profiles too.
# For ProtonVPN's official client (NetShield + built-in kill-switch), additionally
# run: hyprconf addon vpn
networkmanager-openvpn
wireguard-tools

# Security: YubiKey FIDO2 + PIN login (optional hardware)
# Required by `yubikey-fido2-setup` (stowed to ~/.local/bin). The script
# auto-installs these via pacman if missing, so they stay commented here for
# users without a YubiKey. To enable manually: sudo pacman -S libfido2 pam-u2f yubikey-manager
# libfido2          # FIDO2/U2F library (LUKS systemd-cryptenroll, pam_u2f)
# pam-u2f           # PAM module for sudo/login/SSH YubiKey auth
# yubikey-manager   # ykman CLI: key detection + FIDO2 PIN management

# Security: Secure Boot (signed UKI) — optional, UEFI only
# Required by `hyprconf-secureboot` (stowed to ~/.local/bin). The helper
# auto-installs sbctl via pacman when you run `hyprconf secureboot setup`, so it
# stays commented here for users who don't use Secure Boot. Manual: sudo pacman -S sbctl
# sbctl             # Secure Boot key manager (create-keys/sign/verify/enroll)

